WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.476
Roxy leaned toward Terrell. "I'll be right back," she said.

2
00:00:07.477 --> 00:00:09.432
Terrell's eyes went wide.

3
00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:14.187
"You can't get up while the Miners are pitching, Roxy! It's bad luck."

4
00:00:14.188 --> 00:00:15.915
Roxy rolled her eyes.

5
00:00:15.916 --> 00:00:19.163
"It's about Dale Rivers and Manny Gomez.

6
00:00:19.164 --> 00:00:21.074
They've disappeared.

7
00:00:21.075 --> 00:00:23.238
That's why they're not here today.

8
00:00:23.239 --> 00:00:25.310
I need to find them."

9
00:00:25.311 --> 00:00:30.719
"Oh no!" Terrell said. "Good luck."

10
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.956
After Roxy left, a dark shadow covered the stadium.

11
00:00:34.957 --> 00:00:42.198
The crowd looked up and cheered.

12
00:00:42.199 --> 00:00:47.243
"Whoa," Jack said. "That's cool!"

13
00:00:47.244 --> 00:00:49.970
Roxy arrived at Police Headquarters.

14
00:00:49.971 --> 00:00:53.094
Detective Smith was watching a small monitor.

15
00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:57.385
"You have work to do, Detective." Roxy shook her head.

16
00:00:57.386 --> 00:01:01.327
"I can't believe you're watching Cooltube videos!"

17
00:01:01.328 --> 00:01:03.691
Detective Smith rolled his eyes.

18
00:01:03.692 --> 00:01:07.784
"I'm not watching Cooltube videos, Rocket Girl.

19
00:01:07.785 --> 00:01:12.998
I'm watching a security video from Metro City Stadium's parking lot. Take a look."

20
00:01:12.999 --> 00:01:15.870
Roxy leaned in to watch the video.

21
00:01:15.871 --> 00:01:19.102
She saw Dale Rivers and Manny Gomez talking.

22
00:01:19.103 --> 00:01:23.604
A dark shadow spread across the parking lot.

23
00:01:23.605 --> 00:01:26.288
The two baseball players looked up.

24
00:01:26.289 --> 00:01:28.504
They seemed scared.

25
00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:33.048
Then they quickly floated up and off the screen.

26
00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:35.937
"Where did they go?" Roxy asked.

27
00:01:35.938 --> 00:01:40.395
"Did someone—or something—take them?"

28
00:01:40.396 --> 00:01:43.968
Detective Smith shook his head. "I don't know."

29
00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:50.130
The detective's phone beeped. "Hello?" His face grew pale.

30
00:01:50.131 --> 00:01:54.164
"What? Oh no, that's terrible!"

31
00:01:54.165 --> 00:01:56.478
"Uh-oh," Roxy thought.

32
00:01:56.479 --> 00:02:00.983
Her watch beeped.

33
00:02:00.984 --> 00:02:04.247
She opened it and saw Terrell.

34
00:02:04.248 --> 00:02:07.397
"What's going on?" Roxy asked.

35
00:02:07.398 --> 00:02:11.430
"Roxy—I mean Rocket Girl," Terrell said.

36
00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:13.904
"You need to come back to the stadium!

37
00:02:13.905 --> 00:02:16.416
There's a giant baseball floating over it.

38
00:02:16.417 --> 00:02:19.020
At first I thought it was just a balloon.

39
00:02:19.021 --> 00:02:22.256
But now it's sucking up all the Miners!"

40
00:02:22.257 --> 00:02:27.757
"I'll be right there!" Roxy closed her watch and flew off.

41
00:02:27.758 --> 00:02:29.806
Detective Smith put down his phone.

42
00:02:29.807 --> 00:02:39.572
"There's a problem at the stadium, Rocket Girl. We have to . . . Rocket Girl?"

43
00:02:39.573 --> 00:02:44.424
Roxy gulped. An enormous baseball was floating over the stadium.

44
00:02:44.425 --> 00:02:47.079
On the field below, she saw a man.

45
00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.734
He wore a Miners uniform and held a megaphone in one hand.

46
00:02:50.735 --> 00:02:53.164
In the other hand, he held a large bat.

47
00:02:53.165 --> 00:02:54.956
It was silver and shiny.

48
00:02:54.957 --> 00:02:56.934
Sparks shot from it.

49
00:02:56.935 --> 00:03:00.136
"That's Fitz Hitz," Roxy said.

50
00:03:00.137 --> 00:03:04.366
"Why is he on the field? He was kicked off the Miners."

51
00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:09.129
"Hello to all my fans!" Fitz grinned.

52
00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:13.774
"The rest of the team is, uh, tied up right now.

53
00:03:13.775 --> 00:03:16.527
But luckily you have me.

54
00:03:16.528 --> 00:03:21.752
And I have my new invention: the Blast Bat.

55
00:03:21.753 --> 00:03:28.954
I will happily play the Lumbertown Loggers—all by myself!"

